      "title": "LC Model Optimizer ⚡",
      "properties": {
        "lc_note": {
          "source": "en",
          "texts": {
            "en": {
              "text": "## 🛑🚫✋ Run the report first!\n- **Settings > LC123 Settings ⚙️ > Optimization > System & Model Optimization Report**. It tests your machine in about 10 seconds.\n- The optimizer reads that report to pick the right files and speed-ups for YOUR card. No report = Comfy's default files.\n\n**LC Model Optimizer ⚡**\n- It replaces your model, text encoder and VAE loaders. One node, the first thing in the graph.\n- Pick the **base model** (Krea 2, Z-Image, Qwen-Image, SDXL, etc.).\n- Pick a **goal**:\n    - **Quality:** closest to the full model.\n    - **Optimal:** fast and near identical (the default, and the one most people want).\n    - **Fast:** the fastest that still looks right.\n- Leave every file on **★ Recommended** and hit Run. That's it.\n- Missing a file? It shows as **⬇ Download** and grabs it on the first run (check the console, big files take a while).\n- Want your own file (a finetune, a merge, Krealism)? Click the picker and choose it. Your files that match the base model are listed first.\n- Using something it doesn't know? Set the base model to **Custom**, pick your files, and the speed-ups still apply.\n- 💡 Leave **speed_ups** on **Auto**. It only turns on what actually passed the test on your machine. Manual is for people who like to tinker.\n\n**Read the panel on the node before you run**\n- ✅ the file is on disk · ⬇️ it will download · 📦 it comes from the checkpoint.\n- It shows your time per step and whether the model fits on your card.\n- ⚠️ means a file doesn't belong to the base model (e.g. the wrong text encoder). It will still let you run it, but expect errors or bad results.\n\n**LC Model Optimizer Video ⚡**\n- The same thing for video (MiniMax H3, LTX 2.5 / 2.3), plus the audio VAE and the latent upscaler.\n- A part the model doesn't use says **not used by**. Leave it wired, it does no harm.\n\n---\n"
            }
          },
          "titles": {
            "en": "LC Model Optimizer ⚡"
          }
        },
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "English ✏️",
        "## 🛑🚫✋ Run the report first!\n- **Settings > LC123 Settings ⚙️ > Optimization > System & Model Optimization Report**. It tests your machine in about 10 seconds.\n- The optimizer reads that report to pick the right files and speed-ups for YOUR card. No report = Comfy's default files.\n\n**LC Model Optimizer ⚡**\n- It replaces your model, text encoder and VAE loaders. One node, the first thing in the graph.\n- Pick the **base model** (Krea 2, Z-Image, Qwen-Image, SDXL, etc.).\n- Pick a **goal**:\n    - **Quality:** closest to the full model.\n    - **Optimal:** fast and near identical (the default, and the one most people want).\n    - **Fast:** the fastest that still looks right.\n- Leave every file on **★ Recommended** and hit Run. That's it.\n- Missing a file? It shows as **⬇ Download** and grabs it on the first run (check the console, big files take a while).\n- Want your own file (a finetune, a merge, Krealism)? Click the picker and choose it. Your files that match the base model are listed first.\n- Using something it doesn't know? Set the base model to **Custom**, pick your files, and the speed-ups still apply.\n- 💡 Leave **speed_ups** on **Auto**. It only turns on what actually passed the test on your machine. Manual is for people who like to tinker.\n\n**Read the panel on the node before you run**\n- ✅ the file is on disk · ⬇️ it will download · 📦 it comes from the checkpoint.\n- It shows your time per step and whether the model fits on your card.\n- ⚠️ means a file doesn't belong to the base model (e.g. the wrong text encoder). It will still let you run it, but expect errors or bad results.\n\n**LC Model Optimizer Video ⚡**\n- The same thing for video (MiniMax H3, LTX 2.5 / 2.3), plus the audio VAE and the latent upscaler.\n- A part the model doesn't use says **not used by**. Leave it wired, it does no harm.\n\n---\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
